  "schema_version": "language-detection-1",
  "comment": "Decision 111: the document language relatex detects from the text it read when the source declares none (no babel, polyglossia, \\DocumentMetadata lang or language class option). Each language lists frequent function words of its own; the lists are disjoint, and a word common in another listed language (or in English mathematical prose: on, in, an, is, do, per, non, et, sin) is in none. The detection is used only when it is certain: enough words, almost all of them in the language's script, a large share of them frequent words of the winner, and the winner far ahead of the runner-up. Otherwise the export keeps the English default and the language stays an author item.",
